WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:14.515
eyes filled with tears.

2
00:00:14.535 --> 00:00:18.198
"Please don't hurt my friends," she whimpered.

3
00:00:19.038 --> 00:00:22.060
"I didn't tell you talk to me," Morb snarled.

4
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.501
"Talk to them.

5
00:00:23.521 --> 00:00:26.263
Or would you rather get this over with quickly?"

6
00:00:27.144 --> 00:00:29.225
Gliss looked at Darb, Zann, and Perda.

7
00:00:29.946 --> 00:00:32.848
Suddenly her eyes widened, and she stood straight up.

8
00:00:33.536 --> 00:00:36.338
"Yes, I want to say something."

9
00:00:36.358 --> 00:00:41.420
"Fine. Hurry up," Morb said, turning away to fiddle with his contraption.

10
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:47.304
"I just want to say you've been the best friends ever," Gliss said loudly.

11
00:00:47.324 --> 00:00:50.846
"It's been fun going on adventures with you and stuff.

12
00:00:51.886 --> 00:00:56.989
Perda, you're the bravest person I know, and probably the smartest too.

13
00:00:57.689 --> 00:00:59.610
Although Zann is awfully smart too.

14
00:01:00.291 --> 00:01:02.332
He always seems to figure things out.

15
00:01:03.228 --> 00:01:07.330
And Darb, well, you probably know how special I think you are."

16
00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:09.591
Her voice softened for a moment.

17
00:01:10.371 --> 00:01:16.514
Then she cleared her throat and continued talking, describing all the adventures they'd had over the past few

18
00:01:16.574 --> 00:01:19.735
months. Zann stared at her, astonished.

19
00:01:20.515 --> 00:01:21.436
What had come over her?

20
00:01:22.136 --> 00:01:23.697
Gliss never talked this much!

21
00:01:24.537 --> 00:01:25.918
Even Morb seemed surprised.

22
00:01:26.638 --> 00:01:30.800
He turned away from the contraption to gaze at Gliss with his mouth hanging open.

23
00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:32.540
"What's wrong with her?"

24
00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.041
Perda muttered in Zann's ear.

25
00:01:34.741 --> 00:01:38.582
Before he could answer, he spotted sudden movement out of the corner of his eye.

26
00:01:39.342 --> 00:01:42.823
A rope flew out of the rocks at the base of the Seeing Stone.

27
00:01:43.604 --> 00:01:48.145
It looped over Gliss and yanked her off her feet and right over the edge of the plateau!

28
00:01:49.025 --> 00:01:50.446
A nomad popped into view.

29
00:01:50.466 --> 00:01:52.026
"Catch her!"

30
00:01:52.406 --> 00:01:52.946
she shouted.

31
00:01:53.727 --> 00:01:56.667
Several other nomads jumped out and broke Gliss' fall.

32
00:01:57.368 --> 00:01:58.468
They quickly untied her.

33
00:01:59.188 --> 00:02:01.729
Now Zann knew why Gliss had started babbling.

34
00:02:02.469 --> 00:02:06.610
She saw the nomads sneaking up on the group; she was distracting Morb!

35
00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:08.831
Morb roared with fury.

36
00:02:08.851 --> 00:02:10.991
"Give her back!"

37
00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:11.872
Morb shouted.

38
00:02:12.372 --> 00:02:13.552
He rubbed his hands together.

39
00:02:14.312 --> 00:02:15.913
More nomads appeared behind him.

40
00:02:16.613 --> 00:02:22.094
They threw rocks and branches at the contraption, which was now unprotected by any kind of Shield spell.

41
00:02:22.835 --> 00:02:23.795
Morb spun around.

42
00:02:23.815 --> 00:02:25.595
"No!" he cried.

43
00:02:26.115 --> 00:02:27.596
He conjured a new Shield spell.

44
00:02:28.256 --> 00:02:33.099
At the same time, the glowing green shield in front of Zann and his friends blinked off.

45
00:02:34.079 --> 00:02:36.921
A couple of nomads helped Gliss up onto a hoof beast.

46
00:02:37.621 --> 00:02:40.643
More hoof beasts appeared, wild-eyed and terrified.

47
00:02:41.283 --> 00:02:45.585
But they stopped long enough for Zann and the others to fling themselves onto their backs.

48
00:02:46.446 --> 00:02:48.167
"Stop!" Morb cried.

49
00:02:48.947 --> 00:02:53.890
Zann bent low over his animal's neck as he felt magic energy zinging around him.

50
00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:57.952
The entire group was already galloping off in a cloud of dust.

51
00:02:59.676 --> 00:03:03.138
Zann watched several nomads pack tools and clothing into a sack.

52
00:03:03.898 --> 00:03:05.859
"Thank you again for all your help," he said.

53
00:03:05.879 --> 00:03:08.620
"I hope the rest of the search party returns soon."

54
00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:10.320
"We hope so too."

55
00:03:11.161 --> 00:03:14.002
A nomad shot a worried look toward the mouth of the cave.

56
00:03:14.702 --> 00:03:19.264
The kids and their rescuers had been hiding in a cave since escaping from Morb about an hour

57
00:03:19.404 --> 00:03:22.605
earlier. Most of the other nomads had now returned.

58
00:03:23.446 --> 00:03:24.926
Only a few were still missing.

59
00:03:24.946 --> 00:03:27.648
"Are you really moving on so soon?"

60
00:03:27.888 --> 00:03:28.508
Darb asked.

61
00:03:29.248 --> 00:03:30.509
The nomads all nodded.

62
00:03:30.529 --> 00:03:32.750
"It's what we do," one said.

63
00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:40.414
"Besides," another added, "we want to get as deep into the Far Frontier as we can before Her

64
00:03:40.454 --> 00:03:44.196
voice trailed off, and she exchanged a look with some other nomads.

65
00:03:44.216 --> 00:03:48.599
"You want to stay far from whatever is going to happen," Zann finished for her.

66
00:03:48.619 --> 00:03:49.859
"We understand."

67
00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:53.862
A nomad stepped over and put a hand on his shoulder.

68
00:03:54.662 --> 00:03:56.383
"You could come with us," he said.

69
00:03:56.403 --> 00:03:59.697
"Trust me, we know how to remain hidden."

70
00:04:00.658 --> 00:04:02.039
Zann glanced at his friends.

71
00:04:02.719 --> 00:04:06.241
Gliss was huddled beside Darb, still looking relieved to be free.

72
00:04:06.261 --> 00:04:10.044
"We can't," she said, her voice shaking a little.

73
00:04:11.025 --> 00:04:13.567
"We have to try to stop Morb."

74
00:04:13.587 --> 00:04:17.529
"Yes," Zann said, while Perda and Darb nodded.

75
00:04:17.549 --> 00:04:21.552
"I don't know what sort of horror Morb is planning for Magica.

76
00:04:22.092 --> 00:04:24.774
But we have to get back to First City and warn everyone."

77
00:04:24.794 --> 00:04:27.016
"Right," Perda said.

78
00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.681
"But how will we get back without Wyssa?"

79
00:04:29.701 --> 00:04:33.804
"What?" a voice rang out from the cave entrance.

80
00:04:34.564 --> 00:04:36.665
"You're planning to leave me behind?

81
00:04:36.685 --> 00:04:38.486
Ungrateful brats!"

82
00:04:38.506 --> 00:04:42.428
"Wyssa!" Perda cried as the old woman strode in.

83
00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:45.910
"Wait," Zann said, his eyes narrowing.

84
00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:48.412
"Is it really Wyssa this time?

85
00:04:48.832 --> 00:04:52.994
What if He didn't bother to go on, but now everyone looked suspicious.

86
00:04:53.014 --> 00:04:55.836
"Morb told us you were dead," Darb said.

87
00:04:56.616 --> 00:04:57.697
Wyssa rolled her eyes.

88
00:04:57.717 --> 00:05:02.599
"It would take more than a sand beast to take me out," she snapped.

89
00:05:02.619 --> 00:05:05.861
"Obviously Morb didn't do his research.

90
00:05:06.401 --> 00:05:12.144
Everyone knows sand beasts can be tamed if you tickle them in just the right spot on the

91
00:05:12.204 --> 00:05:15.406
lips." Zann felt uncertain.

92
00:05:16.107 --> 00:05:18.228
This person certainly sounded like Wyssa.

93
00:05:18.908 --> 00:05:20.909
But Morb had already tricked them twice.

94
00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.771
Just then several nomads burst in.

95
00:05:24.551 --> 00:05:25.972
The others greeted them with relief.

96
00:05:27.452 --> 00:05:28.613
"Now we are all here!"

97
00:05:29.053 --> 00:05:29.533
one cried.

98
00:05:30.173 --> 00:05:30.934
"We can depart."

99
00:05:31.734 --> 00:05:33.134
One of the newcomers nodded.

100
00:05:33.154 --> 00:05:37.176
"We found your friend," he told the kids, gesturing toward Wyssa.

101
00:05:37.196 --> 00:05:40.458
"Although I imagine she would have found you on her own."

102
00:05:42.318 --> 00:05:44.819
"Yes," another newcomer said with a laugh.

103
00:05:44.839 --> 00:05:49.261
"Anyone who can tame a sand beast can surely do anything!"

104
00:05:50.062 --> 00:05:51.562
That made Zann relax a little.

105
00:05:52.363 --> 00:05:53.203
Perda elbowed him.

106
00:05:53.223 --> 00:05:55.484
"Look at her ring," she whispered.

107
00:05:56.332 --> 00:05:58.533
"That's the ring that Wyssa always wears!"

108
00:05:59.313 --> 00:06:00.113
Perda was right.

109
00:06:00.773 --> 00:06:04.154
The glowing stone peeked out from Wyssa's gnarled hand.

110
00:06:05.175 --> 00:06:06.895
Zann grinned, feeling reassured.

111
00:06:06.915 --> 00:06:08.976
"It must be the real Wyssa."

112
00:06:08.996 --> 00:06:12.437
"Thanks for everything," Wyssa told the nomads.

113
00:06:13.177 --> 00:06:17.898
She pulled some dragon scales out of one pocket and her small contraption out of another.

114
00:06:17.918 --> 00:06:19.859
"We have to go."

115
00:06:20.599 --> 00:06:22.700
She sprinkled the scales over the contraption.

116
00:06:23.529 --> 00:06:27.226
Suddenly Zann and his friends were hurtling back toward First City.
